  "notes": [
    "Gaia DR2 6198594250104473728 and Gaia DR2 6242065813132837376 are the two main-text Sagittarius dSph scattering candidates (T:p7-b2; T:p13-b0), drawn from the Marchetti et al. (2019)-based unbound selection with P_ub > 0.5 (T:p2-b15, T:p2-b16). Gaia DR2 5229262874909180928, Gaia DR2 6255724732546338688, and Gaia DR2 6277913053288720512 are the alternative-selection Sagittarius dSph candidates (T:p10-b3; T:p13-b0), with P_ub > 0.9 (T:p9-b68). Positive scattering evidence is not confirmed with Anders et al. distances (T:p7-b6, T:p10-b4), and the latter three are flagged there as possible spurious astrometry; this affects the scattering follow-up, not their status as prior unbound-candidate follow-ups. The text abbreviates these sources to the first eight Gaia DR2 ID digits, while T:p13-b0 gives the full identifiers.",
    "Gaia DR2 6198594250104473728: Table C4 (T:p13-b0) reports P_ub, explicitly the probability of being unbound from the Milky Way potential; no separate bound probability, individual galactocentric radius, or Galactic rest-frame speed is reported for this source. Two independent heliocentric distances are retained because the paper reports both Marchetti et al. (2019) and Anders et al. (2019) values.",
    "Gaia DR2 6242065813132837376: Target Gaia DR2 6242065813132837376 is the second row of Table C4 (T:p13-b0). The table reports P_ub, the probability of being unbound from the Milky Way potential, not a bound probability; no bound probability is reported. Two independent heliocentric distance estimates are reported, from Marchetti et al. (2019) and Anders et al. (2019), so both are retained without choosing a preferred value.",
    "Gaia DR2 5229262874909180928: Table C4 gives the source's phase-space data and both distance estimates. The source appears in the Appendix A alternative selection; Appendix A reports positive scattering evidence for this star for θ0 = 0.36, but provides no additional eligible quantity. No individual galactocentric radius or total Galactic-rest-frame speed is reported for this star.",
    "Gaia DR2 6255724732546338688: The target star is one of the Table C4 stars discussed in appendix A (alternative selection with P_ub > 0.9). The table reports P_ub, the probability of being unbound, not a bound probability, so only unbound_probability is recorded. The right-ascension proper motion is tabulated as μ_α* = μ_α cos(δ).",
    "Gaia DR2 6277913053288720512: Target Gaia DR2 6277913053288720512 corresponds to shortened identifier 62779130. Table C4 (T:p13-b0) lists it as an Appendix A alternative-selection star with P_ub = 1.00 and a negative parallax. The paper reports positive scattering evidence for this star only when setting θ0 = 0.36 (K ≳ 1), states that the result is not confirmed using Anders et al. (2019) distances, and notes that Anders et al. flag the relevant stars as possible spurious astrometry due to large RUWE (T:p10-b3, T:p10-b4)."
  ]
